Four lengths summing to 20 form a quadrilateral iff every piece is less than 10. The 3-inch piece is fine, so we need all three pieces of the 17-inch stick to be under 10. With cut points $c_1, c_2$ uniform on $[0, 17]$ (the $17 \times 17$ square, area 289), the bad regions are:
- both cuts $\le 7$ (last piece $\ge 10$): a $7 \times 7$ square, area 49;
- both cuts $\ge 10$ (first piece $\ge 10$): area 49;
- $|c_1 - c_2| \ge 10$ (middle piece $\ge 10$): two right triangles with legs 7, total area 49.

They don't overlap, so the good area is $289 - 147 = 142$ and the probability is $\frac{142}{289}$.

**Answer: $\frac{142}{289}$**
